> Just wanted to ask, whether there is any update in lavaan that allows for modeling count data today (as this thread is 8 years old).

No change yet.  Estimating such models requires numerical integration, which is terribly slow in R (and lavaan is written entirely in R).  We just obtained some grant support to modify lavaan's internals with C++, which will enable faster estimation of models requiring numerical estimation methods that are currently infeasible.  So maybe in 4 years this will either be a new feature, or at least lavaan will have been modified in a way that makes it feasible for an interested contributor to provide that extension.

